# What the sitting pins. Plain KEY=value lines (read by lib.sh's load_env, never sourced).
#
# The Rust toolchain the throwaway build uses (design: docs/system-mode.md,
# "Building the programs"). The official standalone archive, so one method
# works on the Ubuntu server and on the Pi, where Debian's rustc (1.85) is too
# old for this crate (it uses `let` chains, stable since 1.88). The build
# downloads it inside its sandbox and refuses it unless its SHA-256 is the
# one below. Raising the version is its own reviewed change: take the new
# hashes from static.rust-lang.org/dist/rust-<version>-<target>.tar.xz.sha256
# and cross-check them against the signed channel manifest.
#
# These two hashes were read from static.rust-lang.org on 1 Nov 2026 and are
# the same hosts' own checksums, so a reviewer should compare them with the
# signed manifest (channel-rust-1.98.1.toml and its .asc) before the first
# real run.
RUST_VERSION=1.98.1
RUST_SHA256_X86_64=5326b36c53de11d148c8f8dab6553a3d1006c2cfd32123683073fad3c302605b
RUST_SHA256_AARCH64=0b514a8cc1cbcd939bff0f151661fe58b6ea5c7a7f645a5098c69e32e8c1e0a2
